==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|menewhile}}, equivalent to {{compound|en|mean|t1=intermediate|while}}. Adverb is by [[ellipsis]] from {{m|en||in the mean while}}, noun being conventionally written as one word after the adjective.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈmiːnwaɪl/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-meanwhile.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈmiːnhwaɪl/|a=non-wine-whine}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The time between two events.
#* Quoted in '''2002''', Stephen C. Ausband, ''Byrd's Line: A Natural History'' (page 37)
#*: In the '''meanwhile''', the surveyors carried the line three miles, which was no contemptible day's work, considering how cruelly they were entangled with briers and gallbushes.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|between-time}}, {{l|en|meantime}}; see also [[Thesaurus:interim]]

====Derived terms====
{{der2|en|in the meanwhile|meanwhile use}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# During the [[time]] that something is happening, {{ngd|often specifically}} in a different place.
#: {{syn|en|in the meantime|meantime|meanwhilst|the while}}
#: {{ux|en|There was a party going on downstairs. '''Meanwhile''', I was reading a book.}}
#* {{RQ:Allingham China Governess|chapter=19|passage='''Meanwhile''' Nanny Broome was recovering from her initial panic and seemed anxious to make up for any kudos she might have lost, by exerting her personality to the utmost. She took the policeman's helmet and placed it on a chair, and unfolded his tunic to shake it and fold it up again for him.}}
# During an [[intervening]] time; from [[now]] until a future time.
#: {{syn|en|meantime|[[until]] [[then]]|for now}}
#: {{ux|en|We’re going on holiday next month; '''meanwhile''', keep working on the project.}}
#* {{quote-hansard|en|date=1 March 1955|speaker=w:Winston Churchill|debate=Defence|house={{w|House of Commons of the United Kingdom|House of Commons}}|columnurl=https://api.parliament.uk/historic-hansard/commons/1955/mar/01/defence#column_1905|column=1905|text=The day may dawn when fair play, love for one's fellow men, respect for justice and freedom, will enable tormented generations to march forth triumphant from the hideous epoch in which we have to dwell. '''Meanwhile''', never flinch, never weary, never despair.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|author=David Osterczy|title=Interknot: Adventures in Internet Dating|isbn=0595325246|page=134|pageurl=https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=0xfe_eEqbXgC&pg=PA134|text=“{{...}} I’m not ignoring you, I’m very sorry, I’ll talk to you soon. '''Meanwhile''', get your tickets.”}}
# [[in contrast|In contrast]] to [[aspect]]s previously mentioned.
#: {{syn|en|at the same time|on the other hand}}
#: {{ux|en|Some songs on the album are beautiful. '''Meanwhile''', others are quite forgettable.}}
#* {{quote-web |en |title=Marina And The Diamonds on 'How to be a Heartbreaker' |date=2013-03-29 |quotee=w:Marina Diamandis |author=Markos Papadatos |work=w:Greek Reporter |url=https://usa.greekreporter.com/2013/03/29/interview-with-marina-and-the-diamonds/ |text=When you are in the studio you don’t have anybody to feed off of, '''meanwhile''' when you are playing live you interact with people and you feel the energy in the room.}}

